    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 there's only the one acceptance test class (plus base/helper), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event while keeping the existing human-readable audit line intact.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an immutable `record` value object `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}` in declaration order matching the spec. Its factory `of(seq, owner)` reads the owner's **primary identifier** rather than the customer-code field directly, so the event's carried identifier follows the primary identifier as it evolves.\n\n2. **`Owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()`** (new accessor) \u2014 the single source of truth for \"the owner's current primary identifier.\" Today it returns `getCustomerCode()`; when the customer code is later unified into a member id, only this one method changes and the audit event automatically carries the member id instead \u2014 no change to the event type or logger.\n\n3. **`OwnerAuditLogger.created()`** \u2014 still emits the original `owner created \u2026` line, then additionally emits the structured event serialized to JSON via a shared Jackson `JsonMapper`. A per-component `AtomicLong` (`incrementAndGet()`) gives `seq` a strictly monotonic value across creates.\n\nEach piece sits where it belongs: the identifier abstraction on the domain entity, the immutable event as its own value type, and the sequence + emission concern in the audit logger. The controller call site (`ownerAuditLogger.created(owner)`) was left untouched.\n\nVerified output:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-18 membershipLevel=1 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
